5	   "where": "AC-61 (L1565) vs AC-171 (L1500), AC-14 (L1489) and Tuning Knobs door area_max row (L1204)",
6	   "issue": "The ADR-0007 sync made published knob ranges guidance only. AC-171 lists door `area_max` 32-128 among the knobs where one step outside the range is NOT refused at boot. AC-61 still requires `DOOR_AREA_MAX` to reject `area_max` 31 and 129 in BOOTING. The two ACs contradict each other on the same values. The `area_max` safe range is the cited Graph `A_HOLE_MAX` range 32-128, so it is a published range. An implementer cannot satisfy both.",
7	   "fix": "Edit AC-61 to match the sync. `area_max` 0 stays a boot refusal (named invariant, because D.5 divides by it). A value above 128 is refused only if the 128 ceiling is declared as a schema bound (`CONTENT_FIELD_RANGE`). 31 and 129 are not boot errors and appear only in the ADVISORY range report. Alternatively, drop door `area_max` from AC-171's list and state in the D.5 row that 32 and 128 are structural invariants. Pick one and make AC-61, AC-171, L668 and L1204 agree."
8	  },
9	  {
10	   "where": "LY-26 a rule (2) (L305) and AC-7 (L1478)",
11	   "issue": "Both still say the dev `dump-save` renders each 64-bit value as an exact-width 16-character lowercase hex string, and AC-7 asserts it. ADR-0006 section 1.3 item 4 and Save/Load (L181, amended in the same sync) say the dump renders any int of magnitude 2^53 or more as a lowercase decimal string. Two 32-bit halves are plain ints below 2^32, so they appear as ints and not as hex. The sync amended the encoding sentence but left the hex-in-dump clause and AC-7's assertion contradicting its own source ADR. AC-7 would fail against an ADR-conformant dump.",
12	   "fix": "Reword rule (2) so hex is the Save/Load header form only, and the dump form follows ADR-0006 section 1.3 (decimal string for ints of 2^53 or more, plain ints for halves). Rewrite the dump clause of AC-7 to assert the round trip through that dump format with `welded_at_T`/`cut_at_T` of 2^53+1. Keep the clause that the snapshot stores halves only if Layout chooses halves; say so explicitly (see advisory on halves)."
